ugh to likely win the trick or force out top cards (Aces or 2s) from the opponents. You should save your pair of 2s to beat Aces or to regain control later, and keep the Rocket as your ultimate insurance. Passing is too passive given your strong hand and need for initiative.\n\nReason: The pair of Kings efficiently beats the pair of 9s without wasting the top-tier pair of 2s. This allows you to potentially win the initiative to play your lowest single card (6). If the Kings are beaten, you still have the pair of 2s and the Rocket to regain control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠K", "♣K"]}'}
